        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ridley Scott, Steven Zaillian, Frank Lucas, Richie Roberts\n- Works: American Gangster\n- Places: La Grange, North Carolina, Harlem, the United States, Vietnam\n- Topics: biographical crime films, heroin smuggling, drug trafficking\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Lucas was born on September 9, 1930.\n- Frank Lucas is an American former drug trafficker who operated in Harlem during the late 1960s and early 1970s.\n- Frank Lucas was from La Grange, North Carolina.\n- Frank Lucas smuggled heroin into the United States on American service planes returning from the Vietnam War.\n- Detective Richie Roberts led the task force that detained Frank Lucas.\n- American Gangster is a 2007 American biographical crime film.\n- Ridley Scott directed and produced American Gangster.\n- Steven Zaillian wrote American Gangster.\n- American Gangster is fictionally based on the criminal career of Frank Lucas.",
